From: Mostafa Saleh <smostafa@google.com>
Date: Wed May 27 09:55:57 2026 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ANDROID: KVM: arm64: iommu: Harden map/unmap checks

Make sure that the IOVA and paddr requested are aligned to the page
size.

Bug: 508703583
Change-Id: I1bb170cce84127e544d09df3067a39332aadac65
Signed-off-by: Mostafa Saleh <smostafa@google.com>

[gki6677 reshape note — 2026-11-01, Z.ai]
Reshaped for the 6.6.77 pin (deprecated/android15-6.6-2025-03 @ 8d05d8f2439f):
- Both hunks re-anchored: the pin tree predates the per-API idmap-domain
  guards (ddb4101bc0ab), so the "if (domain_id == KVM_IOMMU_DOMAIN_IDMAP_ID)"
  context lines of the original hunks do not exist here. The guards are
  inserted at the same logical position (after the overflow check, before
  handle_to_domain()).
- Error codes adapted to the pin contract: kvm_iommu_map_pages() on the pin
  returns 0 on every error path (callers read it as size_t mapped-count), so
  the misalignment guard returns 0 — the source branch's "return -EINVAL"
  would be read back as a huge mapped count. Semantics of the fix unchanged:
  misaligned IOVA/paddr never reach kvm_iommu_ops->{map,unmap}_pages.
- The vulnerable kvm_iommu_map_sg() path of the sibling fix CVE-2026-58846
  does not exist on the pin (divergence list D5).
Verified: git apply --check + apply on the pin tree; patched map_pages /
unmap_pages bodies compared against the upstream source branch.

Origin: android.googlesource.com/kernel/common 6bc773e9c9f8ec6c5c431934462badbbb7d21767
CVE: CVE-2026-58941 (Android security bulletin 2026-09, kernel component table)

---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/iommu/iommu.c b/arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/iommu/iommu.c
index 90a8246..978e86c 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/iommu/iommu.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/iommu/iommu.c
@@ -497,6 +497,9 @@ size_t kvm_iommu_map_pages(pkvm_handle_t domain_id, unsigned long iova,
 	    iova + size < iova || paddr + size < paddr)
 		return 0;
 
+	if (!IS_ALIGNED(iova | paddr, pgsize))
+		return 0;
+
 	domain = handle_to_domain(domain_id);
 	if (!domain || domain_get(domain))
 		return 0;
@@ -593,6 +596,9 @@ size_t kvm_iommu_unmap_pages(pkvm_handle_t domain_id,
 	    iova + size < iova)
 		return 0;
 
+	if (!IS_ALIGNED(iova, pgsize))
+		return 0;
+
 	domain = handle_to_domain(domain_id);
 	if (!domain || domain_get(domain))
 		return 0;
